                                        <div class="tab-pane fade active show" id="pills-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Introduction"><p>The school of Management studies (SOMS) started its academic operations in 1987 with the launch of Diploma in Management as a pilot programme of the University.</p>
<b>VISION</b>
<p>The vision of SOMS is in line with the overall vision of the University in providing seamless and sustainable learner-centric quality education. It also stresses on the skill up gradation of the working professional and provide lifelong learning opportunities in area specific domains like leadership, entrepreneurial skill and professional competence.</p>
<b>MISSION</b>
<p>The mission of the school is to impart knowledge by:<br/>
1- Developing programmes and courses keeping in view the developments taking place in the business world and society at large;<br/>
2- Designing programmes which enrich the knowledge base of the learners and help in
building the competitive advantage;<br/>
3- Sharing the professional skills through collaborative programmes;<br/>
4-Building a strong research base and open new areas of research and development.</P><br/></div>

                                        
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Aboutus"  ><p>The School of Management Studies, began its academic operations in 1987 with the launch of Diploma in Management as a pilot programme of the University. The School comprises of Management and Commerce Disciplines.  The School, at present offers 15 programmes in Management and 10 programmes in Commerce.</p>
<p>The IGNOU Management Programme is one of the leading Management Programmes in the world and imparts quality flexible education at the doorstep of the learners.</p>
<p>The School follows a multimedia approach in programme delivery. It comprises of self-learning printed course material packages supporting audio-video programmes, face to face interaction with academic counselors at study centres, assignment for assessment and feedback, telecast of video programmes on Doordarshan, broadcast of audio / video programmes through Gyan Vani (interactive radio counseling) and teleconferencing through Gyan Darshan and DTH. The School adopts many other learner friendly features available on IGNOU platform.</p>
<p>The programmes offered by the School are designed in modular format offering maximum flexibility to the learners including multiple exit points. In recent years the school has collaborated with various apex institutions to develop programmes catering to the needs of specific target groups. School has plans to develop programmes in various emerging areas to address the country’s need of trained and qualified workforce.</p>
<p>The School of Management Studies has been established to provide developmental avenue for working personnel and professionals for acquiring management qualifications to upgrade and refine their managerial skills, capabilities, and orientation. The School aims to impart lifelong learning opportunities to the learners in the specific domains like leadership, entrepreneurial skills, and professional competence. The Programmes offered by the School are useful and geared to fulfill identified gaps in the corporate and business world. The following are the programmes are on offer:</p>
<p><b>Programmes in Management Discipline:</b></br>
1.	Doctor of Philosophy in Management (PHDMGMT)</br>
2.	Master of Business Administration (MBA)</br>
3.	Master of Business Administration (Online) (MBAOL)</br>
4.	Master of Business Administration (Banking & Finance) (MBF)</br>
5.	Master of Business Administration (Financial Management) (MBAFM)</br>
6.	Master of Business Administration (Human Resource Management) (MBAHM)</br>
7.	Master of Business Administration (Marketing Management) (MBAMM)</br>
8.	Master of Business Administration (Operations Management) (MBAOM)</br>
9.	Post Graduate Diploma in Human Resource Management (PGDIHRM)</br>
10.	Post Graduate Diploma in Financial Management (PGDIFM)</br>
11.	Post Graduate Diploma in Operations Management (PGDIOM)</br>
12.	Post Graduate Diploma in Marketing Management (PGDIMM)</br>
13.	Post Graduate Diploma in Services Management (PGDISM)</br>
14.	Bachelor of Business Administration (Services Management) (BBASM)</br>
15.	Certificate in NGO Management (CNM)</br></p>

<p><b>Programmes in Commerce Discipline:</b></br>
1.	Doctor of Philosophy in Commerce  (PHDCOM)</br>
2.	Master of Commerce  (MCOM)</br>
3.	Master of Commerce (Online)  (MCOMOL)</br>
4.	Post Graduate Diploma in International Business Operations  (PGDIBO)</br>
5.	Bachelor of Commerce  (BCOMF)</br>
6.	Bachelor of Commerce (Online) (BCOMFOL)</br>
7.	Bachelor of Business Administration in Retailing (BBARIL)</br>
8.	Bachelor of Business Administration (BBA)</br>
9.	Diploma in Retailing  (DIRIL)</br>
