                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-9" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="AudioBooks"  ><b>Audio Books</b><br/>

<p>Initially created with a narrative structure, as opposed to verse or dramatic script, audiobooks are adaptations and derivatives of texts initially published in print or online. An audiobook enables the listener to concentrate on the auditory rendition of the text instead of reading the words on a page. Audio books convey an image of accessibility and ease of consumption. Contemporary audiobooks can be digitally downloaded in various audio file formats, including but not limited to MP3, WMA, and AAC. They are compatible with a diverse array of devices, including smartphones, tablets, PCs, and automobiles. Consequently, the content is readily accessible, allowing you to resume just where you paused.<p/>
<p>One can conserve time by engaging with audiobooks while performing household tasks,exercising, driving, cleaning, folding laundry, or shaving. They retain and reinforce nearly as much, if not more, information.<p/>
<p>IGNOU offers audiobooks for its MBA courses, addressing the needs of students who favour learning by listening or require flexible study options. These resources are available on eGyankosh and You Tube.</p></div>
